**Reused Evidence**
No reused evidence items genuinely added chapter-specific 5B evidence here. `E0001` is office-attribution context, but it does not itself bear on economic policy or outcomes.

**New Evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Fiscal Deficit Estimated at 6.4% of GDP in 2022-23","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Finance","publication_date":"2022-02-01","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/pressreleasepage.aspx?prid=1794133&reg=48&lang=2","claim":"The Union Budget 2022-23 set the fiscal deficit at 6.4% of GDP and stepped up capital expenditure by 35.4% to Rs 7.50 lakh crore, with effective capital expenditure at Rs 10.68 lakh crore.","locator":"headline and body paragraphs on fiscal deficit and capital expenditure","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government budget release with exact figures announced in Parliament.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 budget policy choice for the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government through the Union Budget and Finance Ministry.","contrary_evidence":["The fiscal deficit remained elevated, so the policy was pro-growth but not fiscally conservative in an absolute sense.","Budget announcements do not prove implementation on their own."],"lenses":["5B.1","5B.3","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Capital Expenditure Outlay for 2022-23 Increased Sharply by 35.4% with Approximately 67% Spent Between April-December 2022","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Finance","publication_date":"2023-01-31","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1894919&lang=2&reg=3","claim":"By January 2023 the government said about 67% of the 2022-23 capital expenditure outlay had been spent by end-December 2022, alongside 8,964 National Infrastructure Pipeline projects and record road and waterways output.","locator":"headline and opening paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government implementation update with concrete execution figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective evidence on implementation of the 2022 budget within the target period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government’s fiscal and infrastructure execution.","contrary_evidence":["The source is a government self-report, so it may accentuate success.","It reports spending volume, not full welfare impact."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation with India","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-12-23","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/12/19/pr22444-india-imf-executive-board-concludes-2022-article-iv-consultation","claim":"The IMF said the authorities responded to post-pandemic shocks with fiscal measures to support vulnerable groups and front-loaded monetary tightening, with inflation projected at 6.9% in FY2022/23 and risks tilted down.","locator":"press release body and Executive Board Assessment","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous IMF surveillance with explicit findings on policy response and macro conditions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period macroeconomic assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the Modi government and the RBI policy mix under its institutional framework; monetary policy is partly independent, fiscal measures are directly governmental.","contrary_evidence":["The IMF also said public debt sustainability risks had increased.","The source shows stabilization efforts, not a fully successful macro environment."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"India: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report; and Statement by the Executive Director for India","publisher":"International Monetary Fund","publication_date":"2022-12-21","url":"https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/12/21/india-2022-article-iv-consultation-press-release-staff-report-and-statement-by-the-527283","claim":"The IMF staff report said India’s world-class public digital infrastructure was facilitating innovation, productivity improvements and access to services, and that further structural reforms were needed for strong and sustainable growth.","locator":"Summary and staff report summary section","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IMF country report with explicit causal language on digital infrastructure and reforms; still a surveillance document rather than an audit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period structural-growth assessment.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but real attribution to the Modi government because these digital-state capabilities and reform choices were national policy outputs.","contrary_evidence":["The report frames these as enabling conditions, not as proof of broad-based welfare gains.","Structural reforms are recommended as still needed, so the record is unfinished."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.6","5B.7","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indian Economy Continues to Show Resilience Amid Global Uncertainties","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2023-04-04","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2023/04/04/indian-economy-continues-to-show-resilience-amid-global-uncertainties?cid=sar_tt_india_en_ext","claim":"The World Bank said India’s growth for FY2022/23 was estimated at 6.9%, investment was bolstered by the government’s capex push, and inflation averaged around 6.7% for the year.","locator":"press release body and outlook table","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank India update with explicit growth, investment, and inflation figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective but directly on the 2022-23 period that includes the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly attributable to the Modi government’s fiscal choices, though the outcome also reflects private demand and external conditions.","contrary_evidence":["The same source says growth moderated in the second half of FY22/23.","Inflation remained elevated, so the outcome was resilient rather than fully comfortable."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Bank Approves $47 Million Program to Strengthen India’s Public Sector Capability","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-04-27","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/04/27/world-bank-approves-47-million-program-to-strengthen-india-s-public-sector-capability","claim":"The World Bank approved a $47 million project to support Mission Karmayogi and help build the functional and behavioral competencies of about four million civil servants.","locator":"press release body","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank project approval with a concrete capacity-building target and clear 2022 date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period institutional-capacity evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government because Mission Karmayogi is a national government program.","contrary_evidence":["This is capacity-building rather than proof of better policy outcomes.","It speaks to state capability, not to direct competence of every economic appointment."],"lenses":["5B.2","5B.6","5B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Annual Report 2022-23","publisher":"Reserve Bank of India","publication_date":"2023-05-30","url":"https://www.rbi.org.in/scripts/AnnualReportPublications.aspx?Id=1373","claim":"The RBI said CPI inflation remained above the upper tolerance band for 10 successive months in 2022-23, and that government supply-side measures such as excise duty cuts and lower import duties, together with cumulative repo-rate tightening, helped contain price pressures.","locator":"Economic Review, Inflation in India, and central government finances sections","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary central-bank annual report with explicit diagnosis and policy chronology.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on the target year and fiscal year that includes 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Partly direct and partly institutional: government supply-side measures are directly attributable to Modi’s administration, while rate hikes were RBI decisions.","contrary_evidence":["Inflation still exceeded the tolerance band for much of the year.","The report stresses that prices were driven by broad global and domestic shocks, not just domestic policy."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RBI releases the Financial Stability Report, December 2022","publisher":"Reserve Bank of India","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/BS_PressReleaseDisplay.aspx?prid=54955","claim":"The RBI said the Indian economy was facing strong global headwinds but that healthy balance sheets and improving asset quality were supporting financial system resilience, while bank GNPA fell to a seven-year low of 5.0% and NNPA to a ten-year low of 1.3% in September 2022.","locator":"press release highlights","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary RBI stability assessment with clear quantitative balance-sheet indicators.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period financial-sector evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirectly attributable to the Modi government through the broader macro-policy framework; bank balance-sheet repair is shared with RBI and prior reforms.","contrary_evidence":["Financial resilience does not by itself prove broad household prosperity.","The report still flags strong global headwinds."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"India central bank raises key rate, says inflation battle not over","publisher":"ThePrint / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-12-07","url":"https://theprint.in/india/india-central-bank-raises-key-rate-says-inflation-battle-not-over/1252224/","claim":"Reuters reported that the RBI raised the repo rate to 6.25% in December 2022, the fifth straight increase, and said inflation remained elevated.","locator":"lead paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters report on a major macro policy decision, widely corroborated by RBI records.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period monetary-policy evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution only: the RBI is operationally independent, though the government set the wider macro context.","contrary_evidence":["The decision reflects central-bank independence as much as government direction.","Rate hikes are evidence of stabilization pressure, not of economic success."],"lenses":["5B.3","5B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"India | Data","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"best available","url":"https://data.worldbank.org/country/india","claim":"World Bank data show India’s poverty headcount ratio at $3.00 a day (2021 PPP) was 5.3% in 2022.","locator":"Social section, poverty headcount indicator, most recent value (2022)","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official World Bank country data page with the exact 2022 value visible in the indicator table.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 outcome data.","ruler_attribution":"Outcome-only attribution is indirect and mediated by inherited conditions, growth composition, and state implementation.","contrary_evidence":["The page does not itself explain the policy drivers behind the poverty rate.","Poverty still remained nontrivial even after improvement."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Page 24 - World Inequality Report 2022","publisher":"World Inequality Report / WID","publication_date":"2021-12-10","url":"https://wir2022.wid.world/?elqTrackId=2060FE433DCC4F96F7502B3C63FAFE85&elqaid=~~eloqua..type--emailfield..syntax--elqassetid..encodeFor--url~~&elqat=~~eloqua..type--emailfield..syntax--elqassettype..encodeFor--url~~&eq%3B2477=&field_cs_publication_date%5Bmax%5D=&field_cs_publication_date%5Bmin%5D=&field_topics_target_id=All&op=&page=24&search=Blue+Ocean+Strategy&sort_by=created","claim":"The India country sheet says the richest 10% held 57% of national income, the poorest 50% held 13%, and the richest 1% held 22%, describing India as poor and very unequal.","locator":"India country sheet / page 24","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Authoritative inequality report with a precise country sheet and widely cited figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 baseline and close-in context for the 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect attribution only; the figures reflect structural inequality and long-run distribution, not a single-year executive choice.","contrary_evidence":["The figures are from 2021, so they are baseline context rather than a 2022 policy outcome.","The report does not isolate Modi-specific causation."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"A total of 61 applicants approved under Production Linked Incentive Scheme For Textiles out of 67 applications received","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Textiles","publication_date":"2022-04-14","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=1816795&lang=2&reg=3","claim":"The government approved 61 applicants under the textiles PLI scheme, with proposed investment of Rs 19,077 crore, projected turnover of Rs 184,917 crore, and proposed direct employment of 240,134.","locator":"headline and first body paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary implementation announcement with concrete investment and employment targets.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period industrial policy evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government’s industrial policy.","contrary_evidence":["Projected employment is not the same as realized jobs.","The scheme is sector-specific and does not prove economy-wide fairness."],"lenses":["5B.4","5B.6","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Year End Review-2022: Ministry of Rural Development","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Rural Development","publication_date":"2022-12-30","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=1887438&lang=2&reg=48","claim":"The ministry reported that under MGNREGA 11.37 crore households availed employment in 2022, and that 2.11 crore PMAY-G houses had been completed by mid-December 2022.","locator":"Key Initiatives and Achievements section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary year-end implementation report with concrete welfare-delivery figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period welfare and rural-income evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government’s rural-development delivery apparatus, though execution is shared with states.","contrary_evidence":["Household employment under MGNREGA reflects distress as well as support.","The report is a government self-assessment."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Year End Review 2022: Department of Drinking Water and Sanitation, Ministry of Jal Shakti","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Jal Shakti","publication_date":"2022-12-27","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1886953&lang=2&reg=48","claim":"The government said 10.8 crore rural households had tap-water connections under Jal Jeevan Mission by end-2022, and over 1 lakh villages were declared ODF Plus in 2022.","locator":"headline and opening section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government implementation report with concrete infrastructure-delivery figures.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period infrastructure evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government’s national infrastructure and service-delivery program, with implementation shared by states.","contrary_evidence":["Tap-water coverage is a delivery metric, not direct proof of welfare gains.","ODF Plus status is an intermediate step, not a final development outcome."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Year End Review-2022: Ministry of Women and Child Development","publisher":"Press Information Bureau, Government of India / Ministry of Women and Child Development","publication_date":"2022-12-21","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=1885352&lang=2&reg=3","claim":"The ministry reorganized schemes into Mission Saksham Anganwadi and Poshan 2.0, Mission Shakti and Mission Vatsalya, with enlarged outlays and improved nutrition and educational delivery for children and women in 2022.","locator":"opening summary and Mission Saksham Anganwadi and Poshan 2.0 section","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary year-end ministry report with concrete program and budget details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period social-investment evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to the Modi government’s welfare and human-capital policy choices, though outcomes depend on state-level delivery.","contrary_evidence":["The source is a ministry self-report.","Program restructuring does not itself prove improved household welfare."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"India’s factory growth picks up speed in Oct, hiring at 33-month high","publisher":"ThePrint / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-01","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-factory-growth-picks-up-speed-in-oct-hiring-at-33-month-high/1190554/","claim":"Reuters reported that India’s factory activity expanded at a stronger pace in October 2022 and firms hired workers at the fastest pace in nearly three years, with the manufacturing PMI at 55.3.","locator":"lead paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters survey report with a clear jobs and output signal.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 target-period labour and manufacturing evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but meaningful attribution to the Modi government’s industrial and macro environment; the survey itself reflects private-sector activity.","contrary_evidence":["The PMI is a survey, not a government administrative record.","It shows expansion and hiring, not job quality or income distribution."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.9","5B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across official Indian releases, IMF surveillance, World Bank updates, RBI reports, Reuters-syndicated reporting, inequality reporting, and sector program announcements. I retained 15 distinct URLs.

Removed or collapsed:
- Duplicate budget and capital-expenditure releases that repeated the same fiscal figures without adding a new claim.
- Out-of-period 2023-2026 retrospectives unless they directly reported 2022 implementation or 2022-23 outcomes.
- State-level World Bank projects that were informative but too detached from national ruler attribution for the core dossier.
- Generic explainers and commentary that restated the same macro story without adding a materially distinct claim.
- Low-value syndicated duplicates of the same Reuters item.

**Remaining Gaps**
- Direct evidence on Modi personally appointing or empowering named economic professionals in 2022 is thin.
- Corruption/favoritism and politically connected business privilege evidence is still incomplete in this chapter.
- I have strong macro, capex, and social-investment evidence, but weaker direct household-income and wage evidence for 2022.
- More search would help on labor-market quality, median household welfare, and any documented anti-capture or procurement enforcement tied specifically to Modi’s central government in 2022.
